{"segments":[
 {"id": "c07-title-01", "scene": "c07-title", "lang": "en", "text": "Chapter seven. Purpose.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["title"]},
 {"id": "c07-title-02", "scene": "c07-title", "lang": "ar", "text": "مَفْعُولٌ لِأَجْلِهِ", "pause": 0.6, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-rule-01", "scene": "c07-rule", "lang": "en", "text": "The purpose gives the reason for the action.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["show", "hl:gives the reason for the action"]},
 {"id": "c07-rule-02", "scene": "c07-rule", "lang": "en", "text": "To find it, ask why.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["hl:Ask “why?”"]},
 {"id": "c07-rule-03", "scene": "c07-rule", "lang": "en", "text": "It is usually an action noun with tanween, like respect, desire, or seeking.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["hl:action noun", "hl:with tanween"]},
 {"id": "c07-rule-04", "scene": "c07-rule", "lang": "en", "text": "Purpose takes naṣb, so it ends in fatha.", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["hl:Purpose → naṣb, fatha"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-01", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "en", "text": "Example five. The student stood up out of respect.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["en"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-02", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "ar", "text": "وَقَفَ الطَّالِبُ احْتِرَامًا", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["sentence"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-03", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "en", "text": "First, the verb. Stood up. It is a past verb, so it is fixed.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["group:0"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-04", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "en", "text": "Who stood up?", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["ask:1"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-05", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "ar", "text": "الطَّالِبُ", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["group:1", "vowel:1"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-06", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "en", "text": "The student. That is the doer, so it takes damma.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-07", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "en", "text": "Why did he stand?", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ask:2"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-08", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "ar", "text": "احْتِرَامًا", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["group:2", "vowel:2"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-09", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "en", "text": "Out of respect. That is the purpose, so it takes fatha with tanween.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["line:0"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-10", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "en", "text": "Listen to the ending once more.", "pause": 0.3, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex5-11", "scene": "c07-ex5", "lang": "ar", "text": "وَقَفَ الطَّالِبُ احْتِرَامًا", "pause": 0.7, "cues": ["read:2"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex6-01", "scene": "c07-ex6", "lang": "en", "text": "Example six. Zayd studied out of desire for success.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["en"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex6-02", "scene": "c07-ex6", "lang": "ar", "text": "دَرَسَ زَيْدٌ رَغْبَةً فِي النَّجَاحِ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["sentence"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex6-03", "scene": "c07-ex6", "lang": "en", "text": "The verb is fixed, and the doer takes damma.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["group:0", "group:1", "vowel:1"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex6-04", "scene": "c07-ex6", "lang": "en", "text": "Why did he study?", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ask:2"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex6-05", "scene": "c07-ex6", "lang": "ar", "text": "رَغْبَةً", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["group:2", "vowel:2"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex6-06", "scene": "c07-ex6", "lang": "en", "text": "Out of desire. The purpose, so fatha with tanween.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["line:0"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex6-07", "scene": "c07-ex6", "lang": "en", "text": "It ends in a round ta, so there is no extra alif.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex6-08", "scene": "c07-ex6", "lang": "ar", "text": "النَّجَاحِ", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["line:1"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex6-09", "scene": "c07-ex6", "lang": "en", "text": "Success. The small word before it means in. So success comes after a preposition, and it takes kasra.", "pause": 0.5, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-01", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "Example seven. Ali travelled seeking knowledge.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["en"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-02", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "ar", "text": "سَافَرَ عَلِيٌّ طَلَبًا لِلْعِلْمِ", "pause": 0.5, "cues": ["sentence"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-03", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "The verb is fixed. Ali is the doer, with damma.", "pause": 0.25, "cues": ["group:0", "group:1", "vowel:1"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-04", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "Why did he travel?", "pause": 0.6, "cues": ["ask:2"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-05", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "ar", "text": "طَلَبًا", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["group:2", "vowel:2"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-06", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "Seeking. The purpose, so fatha with tanween.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["line:0"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-07", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "ar", "text": "لِلْعِلْمِ", "pause": 0.3, "cues": ["line:1"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-08", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "This word has two parts. The first part means for. It is a small preposition.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-09", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "ar", "text": "العِلْمِ", "pause": 0.3, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-10", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "Knowledge. It comes after a preposition, so it takes kasra.", "pause": 0.5, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-11", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "A tip. Object or purpose? Ask the question.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": ["tip"]},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-12", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "ar", "text": "قَرَأَ زَيْدٌ كِتَابًا", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-13", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "What did he read?", "pause": 0.5, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-14", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "A book. That is the object.", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-15", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "ar", "text": "وَقَفَ زَيْدٌ احْتِرَامًا", "pause": 0.4, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-16", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "Why did he stand?", "pause": 0.5, "cues": []},
 {"id": "c07-ex7-17", "scene": "c07-ex7", "lang": "en", "text": "Out of respect. That is the purpose.", "pause": 0.8, "cues": []}
]}
